cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this plugin, please cite the upstream HarnessMM paper below."
title: HarnessMM DSH Plugin
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/Xiuxiu-6/harnessmm-dsh
abstract: >-
  A DeepSeek Harness Host plugin implementing guarded decision reuse. The model
  authors already-decided tool actions once; actions whose receipt guard holds
  execute through the native tools without another reasoning request, and each
  substitution is certified after the real tool result returns. Derived from the
  HarnessMM research codebase.
keywords:
  - deepseek-harness
  - dsh
  - dsh-plugin
  - harnessmm
  - decision-reuse
  - token-efficiency
references:
  - type: software
    title: "HarnessMM: Recursive Self-Improvement for Harness Token Efficiency"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jiang
        given-names: Yuhua
      - family-names: Xu
        given-names: Chang
      - family-names: Gao
        given-names: Feifei
      - family-names: Zhao
        given-names: Li
    year: 2026
    repository-code: https://github.com/YuhuaJiang2002/HarnessMM
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32813
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Upstream work that this plugin is derived from. The plugin ports the GDR
      and CCS contracts from integrations/deepseek_harness/sar_v2.mjs and
      cot_jev.mjs; see NOTICE for the changes made.
